# Ramification over j = 1728 divides 2 on X₀(N)

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.ord_jBar_sub_1728_dvd_two`
(`ad7b8fd1-51b8-5a26-a7e1-ee7822d46f82`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `e476b002-f8df-5a17-a9fe-04211252881b`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a positive natural number, and work inside the field $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N$ =
[`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldBar N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L111), the
intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ over
$\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` generated by the coefficientwise images, under the
embedding `coeffEmb` induced by $\mathbb Q \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, of the elements of
[`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull N`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), itself the subfield of
$\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb Q)$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor $q$-expansions
`divisorExpansions N`. Let $v$ be a place of this field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the project's
sense, i.e. a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N$ containing the image of
$\overline{\mathbb Q}$, different from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring; for $f$ in the
field, $v.\mathrm{ord}(f) \in \mathbb Z$ is minus the logarithm of the associated
height-one-spectrum adic valuation of $f$. Let $\bar\jmath$ = [`ModularCurve.jBar
N`](def/ModularCurve_MazurStepThreeInputs.html#L43) be the element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N$
given by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Assuming
$v.\mathrm{ord}(\bar\jmath - 1728) > 0$, the conclusion is that $v.\mathrm{ord}(\bar\jmath - 1728)$
divides $2$ in $\mathbb Z$; equivalently, this order is $1$ or $2$.

This is the local statement that the covering $X_0(N) \to X(1)$, read through the inclusion of
function fields over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is at worst quadratically ramified above the elliptic
point $j = 1728$, the point of order two for the modular group. It is one of the inputs to the
ramification count entering the genus formula for $X_0(N)$ and to the description of Riemann–Roch
spaces and regular differentials on the curve, being cited by
[`ModularCurve.genus_modularFunctionFieldBar_eq_genusFormula`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.genus_modularFunctionFieldBar_eq_genusFormula)
among others.

